@* §6.16 (NAV-004) — this is what a Control Panel admin actually lands on for any
   unhandled exception in production: UseExceptionHandler targets it from the
   non-Development branch. It was the untouched Blazor scaffold — unlocalized, in
   Bootstrap `text-danger` rather than the CP's own styles, outside the shell, and
   it printed a paragraph of ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT instructions telling the reader
   how to turn on Development mode. That text is addressed to a developer, not to
   the admin who hit the error, and it advertises how to make the deployment leak
   exception detail. Removed; the reference id stays, because that is the one thing
   worth quoting to support. *@
@page "/Error"
@layout CpShellLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@inject IStringLocalizer<Strings> L

<PageTitle>@L["Error.Title"] · SIMF</PageTitle>

<SimfPageHeader Title='@L["Error.Title"]' />

<div class="simf-panel">
    <p class="simf-panel__text">@L["Error.Text"]</p>

    @if (ShowRequestId)
    {
        <p class="simf-panel__text">
            <strong>@L["Error.RequestId"]:</strong> <code>@RequestId</code>
        </p>
    }

    <p class="simf-panel__action">
        <SimfLink Href="/">@L["Error.Back"]</SimfLink>
    </p>
</div>
